    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T03:07:43Z",
    "body": "Fact from #2031 (branch `issue/2031-rest-adaptive`): the motion-crate generator `camcraft_motion::machining2d::rest_adaptive(region, params, stock)` takes the remaining stock as a `RestStock`, which this task is the producer of.\n\nThe contract it reads (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/rest/stock.rs`):\n\n- `RestStock::from_verified(floors)`: one `StockFloor { z, remaining, uncertain }` per depth the earlier operations are proved to have cut to. A floor claims: inside the pocket, at and above `z`, material stands only inside `remaining` or `uncertain`. Below `z` it says nothing.\n- For a cut depth, every floor at least that deep speaks; a cut depth below every floor is refused by name (\"the remaining stock is not proved at Z...\").\n- `uncertain` stands as material: never entered, cut under the load bound.\n- `RestStock::with_film(mm)` states the proof's resolution (default 0.02 mm): residue thinner than that gets no pass, but still stands for every load reading and no plunge lands on it. A stock read from a grid should set it to about one cell.\n- There is no constructor from an entered tool diameter.\n\nThe Pocket operation's door (`rest2d::rest_strategy`) still refuses Adaptive for rest machining. Lifting it is: build the `RestStock` from the carried stock and call `rest_adaptive`. Limits of the planner are in #2108 and #2109.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
